{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10310": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor, Speech-Language Pathology (Full Time)",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Clinical Instructor, Speech-Language Pathology (Full Time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Instructor, Speech-Language Pathology (Full Time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Reference letters are required, please include at least three references that will provide letters of recommendation on your behalf. Please note that these references will be contacted by email. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500140 Job Title Clinical Instructor, Speech-Language Pathology (Full Time) Position Number F03308 Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Non Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo’s Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology housed within the College of Health Professions invites applications for an Instructor of Speech Language Pathology. The position is a full-time, 9-month faculty position. There is opportunity for advancement to Senior Instructor. Assigned teaching responsibilities include clinical supervision and clinical teaching of Speech-Language Pathology graduate students and may include undergraduate and graduate teaching. Summer teaching and supervision opportunities may be available but are not required. This position is designed for a dynamic educator committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student mentorship and supervision, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Supervision and teaching methods, practices, and strategies should be in accordance with current evidence and best practice guidelines. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and delivery of curriculum that prepares students for careers in speech language pathology. Experience and willingness to work with both pediatric and adult populations preferred. Essential Job Duties Supervise graduate students, unless duties are adjusted to accommodate other responsibilities. Manage 1-2 diagnostic groups each semester, as assigned. Conduct preschool screenings with Clinic Director (an average of 2 per semester) as assigned. Maintain office hours weekly. Assist the Clinic Director with Clinic Forum ( SLP 579, SLP 580) as needed. Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. Additional Duties KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS , AND ABILITIES : Ability to supervise the work of others; Excellent oral and written communication skills; General knowledge of university operations, policies and procedures; Strong interpersonal skills; Ability to effectively communicate complex ideas orally and written. Education and Experience The minimum educational requirement for this position is: Master’s degree in SLP Education substituted for experience? No This position requires: 3 years clinical and/or supervisory experience. Experience substituted for education? No Preferred Education and Experience Licenses, Certification or Registrations Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications required for this position include: Current ASHA Certification, must be maintained Alabama State License or be eligible to obtain Alabama State Licensure prior to beginning employment, must be maintained Must possess or complete required supervisor-related training for speech language pathology Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications preferred for this position include: None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 03/20/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Reference letters are required, please include at least three references that will provide letters of recommendation on your behalf. Please note that these references will be contacted by email. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information FULL POSITNG The University of Montevallo’s Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology housed within the College of Health Professions invites applications for an Instructor of Speech Language Pathology. The position is a full-time, 9-month faculty position. There is opportunity for advancement to Senior Instructor. Assigned teaching responsibilities include clinical supervision and clinical teaching of Speech-Language Pathology graduate students and may include undergraduate and graduate teaching. Summer teaching and supervision opportunities may be available but are not required. This position is designed for a dynamic educator committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student mentorship and supervision, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Supervision and teaching methods, practices, and strategies should be in accordance with current evidence and best practice guidelines. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and delivery of curriculum that prepares students for careers in speech language pathology. Experience and willingness to work with both pediatric and adult populations preferred. ESSENTIAL JOB DUTIES : 1. Supervise graduate students, unless duties are adjusted to accommodate other responsibilities. 2. Manage 1-2 diagnostic groups each semester, as assigned. 3. Conduct preschool screenings with Clinic Director (an average of 2 per semester) as assigned. 4. Maintain office hours weekly. 5. Assist the Clinic Director with Clinic Forum ( SLP 579, SLP 580) as needed. Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS , AND ABILITIES : Ability to supervise the work of others; Excellent oral and written communication skills; General knowledge of university operations, policies and procedures; Strong interpersonal skills; Ability to effectively communicate complex ideas orally and written; EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE : The minimum educational requirement for this position is: Master’s degree in SLP Education substituted for experience? No This position requires: 3 years clinical and/or supervisory experience. Experience substituted for education? No LICENSES , CERTIFICATIONS , OR REGISTRATIONS : Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications required for this position include: · Current ASHA Certification, must be maintained · Alabama State License or be eligible to obtain Alabama State Licensure prior to beginning employment, must be maintained · Must possess or complete required supervisor-related training for speech language pathology Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications preferred for this position include: None Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10218 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts References Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
