    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10524": {
      "title": "Student Office Assistant, Counseling Services",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Student Office Assistant, Counseling Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Office Assistant, Counseling Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Student Office Assistant, Counseling Services Department Counseling Services Rate of Pay $8 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week 10 Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Work-Study General Description The purpose of this position is to provide office administrative support for Counseling Services (CS), to assist with departmental events and programs, and help with the operation of the Campus Food Pantry. Essential Job Duties 1) Provide friendly and helpful customer service by welcoming and assisting clients and visitors, answering and directing phone calls, and taking and delivering messages. 2) Schedule appointments and meetings for CS professional staff and graduate assistants. 3) Follow CS procedures in order to maintain confidentiality. 4) Help CS Staff with organizing and executing CS Events and prevention initiatives. As your schedule allows, attendance at those events is required. 5) Assist in the operation of the Campus Food Pantry. Duties include, but are not limited to, sorting and shelving donations, creating food boxes, helping with fundraisers and/or donation drives. 6) Assist CS director and professional staff with administrative tasks as assigned. 7) Keep CS office space organized and clean. 8) Assist with other duties as assigned. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1) Be self-directed and motivated. 2) Maintain behavior consistent with being a role model to the UM community. 3) Adhere to appropriate ethical and legal requirements concerning confidentiality and client care. 4) Interact with clients and the UM community in an effective way. 5) Dress appropriately for a professional setting. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 08/20/2026 Open Date 09/04/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Student Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Letter of Application University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
