    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10478": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Media Relations",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Assistant Director of Media Relations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Media Relations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number S1500766 Job Title Assistant Director of Media Relations Position Number P22567 Division Athletics Department Sports Information FLSA Non-Exempt Salary Grade 113 Salary Classification Admin/Professional Annual Salary Range Hourly Salary Range $16.62 - $22.16 Employment Status Full Time 12 Mos Regular General Description The purpose of this position is to assist the Director of Media Relations with preparation and dissemination of information to the University community and to local and state media; promote and publicize sports-related stories and events. Essential Job Duties 1. Assist the Director of Media Relations with game day operations; oversee press row/press box management for home athletics events in the absence of the Director of Media Relations, including supervision of student assistants. 2. Assist the Director of Media Relations with the production of all sports information materials to the media. 3. Assist the Director of Media Relations with the coordination and management of information pertaining to Athletics on the University website. 4. Assist the Director of Media Relations with marketing and promotions projects, including oversight of the department’s fan engagement app. 5. Assist with developing and implementing office policies for the Sports Information Department. 6. Assist with the organization of publications production flow and advertising for publications. 7. Assist in managing updates to the athletic department website and social media account (e.g. Facebook, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube, etc.) for all athletic teams and department. 8. Create press releases, game notes, and stories for publication. 9. Assist in maintaining team and individual statistics. 10. Assist with the coordination of media coverage for all home and away athletic events. 11. Provide leadership, evaluate, and supervise direct reports in performing duties as charged. 12. Assist the department with the planning and execution of special and annual events, including but not limited to Hall of Fame, Student-Athlete End of Year recognition, etc. Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. Additional Duties The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of and compliance with NCAA and conference rules and regulations; Knowledge of media practices and procedures; Knowledge of statistics, rules and regulations for the sports to be covered; Knowledge of computerized statistical packages and desktop publishing equipment; Ability to communicate effectively; Ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines; work nights and weekends as required. Education and Experience The educational requirement for this position is: Bachelor’s degree Education substituted for experience? No This position requires: 1-3 years of related experience. Experience substituted for education? No Licenses, Certification or Registrations Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications required for this position include: • Valid driver’s license • Acceptable driving record Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications preferred for this position include: • None Environmental Working Conditions Indoor and Outdoor Travel Requirements Number of Vacancies 2 Desired Start Date Physical Requirements Standing: Under 1/3 of the time; walking: Under 1/3 of the time; sitting: Up to 