    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10078": {
      "title": "Career Center Student Office Assistant",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Career Center Student Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Career Center Student Office Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Career Center Student Office Assistant Department Career Center Rate of Pay $8 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Work-Study General Description Provide office coverage and administrative support for the Career Development Center. Essential Job Duties 1) Perform various clerical and office-related tasks. 2) Provide effective customer service by welcoming and assisting visitors. 3) Make appointments, answer questions, and offer relevant information. 4) Answer phones, direct calls, and take accurate phone messages. 5) Originate, process, organize, and file confidential documents. 6) Organize and inventory office supplies and other related materials. 7) Assist with departmental events and programs. 8) Help process informational and promotional materials by restocking literature racks, making photocopies, and assembling information packets. 9) Run errands and make deliveries across campus. 10) Perform other relevant duties as assigned. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1) Strong interpersonal communication skills. 2) Responsible, self-directed, and motivated. 3) Organized and detail oriented. 4) Ability to interact with visitors in a friendly, positive, and helpful way. 5) Dress and act appropriately for a professional setting. 6) Ability to use office equipment (computer, copier, printer, multi-line phone system) and applications (word processing, e-mail, internet). 7) Adhere to strict ethical and legal requirements concerning confidentiality and protecting information. 8) Previous clerical and office experience preferred. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 09/10/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Letter of Application Resume University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
