    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10159": {
      "title": "Alumni Events Assistant",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Alumni Events Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Alumni Events Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Alumni Events Assistant Department Alumni Affairs Rate of Pay $8 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status As Needed Student Appointment Type Jobship and Work-Study General Description Provide support to Alumni Affairs staff in successfully coordinating and executing alumni events. May be called upon to handle office tasks. Essential Job Duties 1) Organize, pack, and load items for transport to events. 2) Set up and break down event displays, decorations, etc., at events. 3) Make name tags. 4) Register and collect information from event attendees. 5) Clean up event spaces, and maintain organized storage space for event supplies. 6) Provide courteous and helpful service when working with alumni volunteers and event attendees. 7) Run errands or perform office tasks when needed. 8) Help with events, especially in the evenings and on weekends. Must be available to help with Founders’ Day activities in October and Homecoming events in February. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1) Should possess strong organization skills. 2) Must be self-directed, motivated, punctual, reliable, and demonstrate initiative. 3) Should be able to interact with volunteers, attendees, guests, etc. and represent the alumni constituents in a professional manner. 4) Must be able to take direction from the office staff as well as alumni board volunteers/committee chairs. 5) Ability to dress appropriately for the event being worked. 6) Trustworthy and responsible to handle money. 7) A flexible schedule week-to-week depending on upcoming events is a must. Some nights and weekends will be required. (Can be planned a week or two in advance.) 8) Must be able to lift and carry 20-25 pounds such as coolers, tents, boxes, etc. 9) Should be able to drive a golf cart. 10) Maintain confidentiality. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations Driver’s License preferred. Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 12/15/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
