    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10445": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant II",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant II - Child Study Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant II - Child Study Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Graduate Assistant II - Child Study Center Department Family and Consumer Sciences Rate of Pay $13.00 Hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week 20 hours per week between 7:45am - 2:30pm Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Graduate Assistant General Description The purpose of this position is to assist the teachers in providing a safe, nurturing, and developmentally appropriate environment for the children at the Child Study Center. Essential Job Duties Promote teacher-child relations by helping children adapt to the environment. Be responsible for guidance and self-discipline among children. Build classroom community. Supervise arrival/departure of children. Foster classroom relationships with family members. Assist with and ensure set-up/clean-up of daily routine. Prepare and serve meals and snacks. Exhibit and maintain a child-centered safe and healthy environment in both the indoor and outdoor classrooms. Complete Daily Sheets, Incident Reports, and potential assessments in relation to the children. Complete evaluations on University students. Complete assignments as given by the teachers and/or director. Abide by all policies stated in the Child Study Center Handbook. Assist in other areas as needed. Education and Experience Undergraduate degree with a minimum of a 3.0 grade point average (on 4.0 scale). A minimum of 12 college credits [semester hours] in Family and Consumer Sciences ( FCS ), Early Childhood Education ( ECE ), Child Development (CD), Elementary Education, Early Childhood Special Education ( ECSE ). Course content encompasses child development (physical, language, emotional, cognitive, social) and learning of children birth through kindergarten; family and community relationships; observing, documenting, and assessing young children; teaching and learning; and professional practices and development. Baccalaureate degree in FCS , early childhood education, child development, elementary education or early childhood special education that encompasses child development and learning of children birth through kindergarten; family and community relationships; observing, documenting, and assessing young children; teaching and learning; and professional practices and development. Equivalence is defined as a Baccalaureate’s degree in any discipline with a minimum of 36 college credits [semester hours] in early childhood education, child development, elementary education or early childhood special education that encompasses child development and learning of children birth through kindergarten; family and community relationships; observing, documenting, and assessing young children; teaching and learning; and professional practices and development. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Experience working in a child care center, nursery school, children’s home, family childcare home, or related experience working in an accredited setting. Understanding of developmentally appropriate practices advocated by the National Association for the Education of Young Children. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/19/2026 Open Date 08/03/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10292": {
      "title": "Summer Music & Theatre Office Assistant",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Summer Music &amp; Theatre Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Summer Music & Theatre Office Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Summer Music & Theatre Office Assistant Department Music Rate of Pay $8.00 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship General Description Provide general administrative assistance to faculty in the Music and Theatre Department. Flexible work hours. Essential Job Duties 1. Prepare bulk mailings by printing/coping documents, preparing labels, folding letters, and stuffing envelopes. 2. Organize and file documents. 3. Assist with maintaining, retrieving and filing music collections. 4. Organize office/classroom spaces and equipment. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1. Must have good organization skills. 2. Ability to work independently with little or no supervision. 3. Must have an eye for detail and accuracy. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations None Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 05/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
