    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10158": {
      "title": "Alumni Communications Student Assistant",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Alumni Communications Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Alumni Communications Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Alumni Communications Student Assistant Department Alumni Affairs Rate of Pay $8.00 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship and Work-Study General Description Assist with alumni social media and provide office support for the Alumni Affairs Office. Occasionally assist with events and programs. Essential Job Duties 1) Develop and maintain a social media content planning calendar. 2) Create and curate regular content for UM Alumni Office social media accounts and groups on Facebook, Twitter, Instagram and LinkedIn. 3) Monitor, listen and respond to users’ comments and questions in a timely manner. 4) Manage the general alumni email account. 5) Assist the Alumni Office with the development and assessment of alumni surveys. 6) Provide friendly and helpful customer service by welcoming and assisting visitors, answering and directing phone calls, taking and delivering messages, and general office duties as needed. 7) Maintain confidentiality. 8) Work after-hours and weekend events as necessary. Education and Experience High School Diploma or GED equivalent. Communication Studies, Mass Communication or Marketing major preferred. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 1) Need to be self-directed, motivated, punctual and reliable. 2) Strong communication, PR and writing skills. 3) Possess proficiency with social media, Canva and related software. 4) Maintain behavior consistent with being a representative of the Alumni Office. Dress and act in a professionally appropriate manner. 5) Good interpersonal, customer service skills and ability to interact with visitors, guests and the UM community in an effective way. 6) Photography or videography skills a plus but not required. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations Driver’s license preferred. Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Open Date 12/15/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes a