    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10507": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1500147 Job Title Open Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing Position Number TBD Salary Commensurate with experience FLSA Exempt Employment Status Full Time 9 Mos Regular Appointment Type Full-time Tenure or Non-Tenure Track General Description The University of Montevallo’s Department of Nursing and Health Sciences housed within the College of Health Professions invite applications for a nine-month, OOpen Rank, Instructor (Tenure or Non-tenure Track), Nursing. Assigned teaching responsibilities include undergraduate teaching with prelicensure students in the classroom, lab, and clinical settings. Specifically, the successful candidate will teach maternal child/reproductive health and/or nursing care of children as well as other nursing courses. Summer teaching may be required for this position and compensation will be provided. This position is designed for a dynamic nurse educator committed to excellence in teaching, student mentoring, and scholarly engagement. The successful candidate will participate in academic advising; curriculum development and program assessment; establish an independent line of scholarly activity/research and publish in scholarly journals; and provide service to the program, department, college, university, and community. Essential Job Duties Primary teaching responsibilities are in the undergraduate prelicensure track teaching maternal/child/reproductive health and/or nursing care of children and will include additional nursing courses (including the RN to BSN track courses) based on qualifications. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, scholarship/research, service to the program, department, college, university, and the community. Additional Duties Education and Experience Master’s degree in nursing required; Doctoral degree in nursing is preferred. Preferred Education and Experience Documented experience and excellence in teaching; peer-reviewed publications in translational, human subjects research; evidence of successful advising at the undergraduate level; simulation experience or certified healthcare simulation educator; membership and involvement in professional organizations; familiarity with the AACN Essentials and the Commission of Collegiate Nursing Education organizations. Licenses, Certification or Registrations Must possess an unencumbered registered nursing (RN) license in Alabama, multistate RN license, or be eligible for Alabama RN licensure prior to beginning employment. Maintains American Heart Association BLS HCP certification. Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Open Date 08/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Opportunity Institution. Quick Link https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10501 Lookup Appointment Type Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com HigherEdJobs/Affirmative Action Email List The Academic Network, Inc. MFAD (Minority Faculty Application Database) SREB (Southern Regional Education Board) Birmingham News Shelby County Reporter Birmingham Times Advertisement/Publication Indeed LinkedIn Personal Referral UM Website Agency Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Unofficial Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10056": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant I",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant I - Registrar&#39;s Office Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant I - Registrar's Office Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Graduate Assistant I - Registrar's Office Department Registrar's Office Rate of Pay $12.00 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Graduate Assistant General Description The purpose of this position is to provide office advanced administrative support for the Registrar’s Office. Essential Job Duties Act as one of the first points of contact to students, faculty, staff, parents, and community members to include walk-ins and telephone calls. Provide direct support to students, faculty, staff, parents, and community. Assist the Administrative Assistant in scanning, indexing, and verifying data integrity for the document management system. Occasionally participate in and assist with Preview Day and Orientation information fairs, and other recruitment and informational events on campus. Assist other members of the team during peak times, such as registration, beginning and end of terms, graduation, campus visits, orientations days, etc. Function as an active integral part of the Registrar’s Office and University teams in support of their missions and the UM Strategic plan. Other related duties as assigned. Education and Experience Enrollment in a UM graduate degree program Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Be self-directed and motivated. Adhere to strict ethical and legal requirements concerning confidentiality and protecting information. Must be detail oriented. Ability to interact with students, faculty, and staff in a positive and effective way. Dress appropriately for a professional setting. Ability to use office equipment (Xerox copier and Multi-line Phone system). Must be familiar with MS Office programs. Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations NA Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date 08/20/2025 Open Date 08/05/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
