    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10444": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant I",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant I - Athletic Media Relations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant I - Athletic Media Relations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Graduate Assistant I - Athletic Media Relations Department Athletics Rate of Pay $12.00 hourly FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week 20 hours per week/variable hours Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Graduate Assistant General Description The purpose of this position is to assist in the Athletic Media Relations office with home athletic events and publicizing UM athletic events through print, video, photo, social media and various digital media outlets. Essential Job Duties Contribute original text, photo, and video content for website and social media platforms (e.g., departmental Facebook, Twitter, Instagram, Website). Work in an official capacity at home athletic events (e.g., operating scoreboards, compiling statistics, public address, creative content) Write press releases featuring game recaps, individual awards and recognition, and student-athlete profiles as assigned. Serve as the secondary media relations contact for assigned sports. Assist in the supervision of student-workers and interns. Manage creative content student-workers/interns directly and oversee scheduling. Manage and organize all digital media assets, using Flickr. Assist in creative content planning and development. Suggest content idea and social media ideas. Assist in the planning and execution of Media Days and various content shoots. Assist with special events as assigned. Assist with day-to-day office duties including, website maintenance, digital programs, record keeping/updates, etc. Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree and enrollment in a UM graduate degree program. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Must have excellent communication and grammar skills. (Written and verbal.) Possess proficiency with social media platforms. (Twitter, Facebook, Instagram) Possess proficiency with Microsoft Office 365 Possess proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud Proficient in creative content strategies and skills. (Shoot planning, video, photo, editing etc.) Be self-directed and motivated. Maintain behavior consistent with being a role model to the UM community. Detail-oriented and organized. Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations NA Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/19/2026 Open Date 07/31/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10191": {
      "title": "Montevallo Scholars Literacy Tutor",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal | Montevallo Scholars Literacy Tutor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Montevallo Scholars Literacy Tutor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to Human Resources, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options Position Information Posting Number Job Title Montevallo Scholars Literacy Tutor Department Teaching, Leadership, & Technology Rate of Pay Flat Rate FLSA Non-Exempt Estimated Number of Hours Per Week Employment Status Part Time Temporary Student Appointment Type Jobship General Description Are you passionate about helping young learners thrive in literacy? Join the Montevallo Scholars Literacy Tutor team! As a Literacy Tutor, you’ll provide engaging, twice-weekly after-school tutoring to elementary students during the spring semester and participate in a four-week literacy enrichment program in June 2026. This is a unique opportunity to make a lasting impact while applying your coursework in a supportive, community-focused environment. Essential Job Duties Key Responsibilities: Deliver small-group literacy instruction tailored to students’ needs Support early readers with engaging, research-based strategies Collaborate with teachers and fellow tutors to enhance student learning Commit to consistent attendance and professional conduct Education and Experience Must be admitted to the Teacher Education Program and currently enrolled in Methods Block Courses. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Ideal Candidates: Currently enrolled in Methods Block courses (Early Childhood/Elementary Education) Passionate about literacy and student success Reliable, enthusiastic, and ready to learn through hands-on teaching Preferred Major Licenses, Certification or Registrations Ideal candidates would be currently enrolled in Methods Block courses. Number of Vacancies 9 Desired Start Date Open Date 02/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. EEO Statement UM is an Equal Employment Opportunity Institution Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently a student (having been admitted or enrolled in classes) at the University of Montevallo? Yes No Have you been awarded Federal Work-Study by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents University of Montevallo Human Resources and Risk Management Station 6055 Will Lyman House Montevallo, AL 35115 (205) 665-6055 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/10492": {
      "title": "Vitae Bank 2026-2027 Michael E Stephens College of Business (Pool)",
      "description": "University of Montevallo Applicant Portal Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Vitae Bank 2026-2027 Michael E Stephens College of Business (Pool) Bookmark this Pool | Print Preview | Apply for this Pool Pool Details First Section Name Vitae Bank 2026-2027 Michael E Stephens College of Business Job Title Vitae Bank 2026-2027 Michael E Stephens College of Business College College of Business Division Academic Affairs Position Type Temporary Faculty Part-time Salary Competitive Adjunct Rate FLSA Exempt Job Description Summary Teach courses as assigned by the Department Chair. Temporary faculty in the following areas: accounting; data analytics; Computer Science; economics; finance; information systems; management; marketing; and several other disciplines. The Adjunct Instructor for the Michael E. Stephens College of Business serves as an official representative of the University, promoting a positive first-impression by adopting and demonstrating a collegial, customer-service approach to students, parents, faculty, staff and other members of the University community. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in teaching discipline from a regionally accredited institution or equivalent in professional experiences. Special Instructions Summary EEO Statement The University of Montevallo does not discriminate against job applicants based on their national origin or citizenship or immigration status. Because of the costs associated with visa sponsorship/transfer, the University typically will not sponsor applicants for a work visa or transfer of an existing visa. No commitment for visa assistance and/or sponsorship can be made until a thorough search is conducted, including a proper and methodical review of all applicants. UM is an EO/D/V Employer Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job